<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Tags VFEP's warcasket minigun for the man in black's kind (Defs/PawnKindDefs/
    StrangerInBlack_Medic.xml): vanilla's weapon generation picks by weaponTags, and the
    minigun's own tags (WarcasketAll, WarcasketHeavy) are shared with the other heavy guns, so
    a tag of ours on this one def is what makes the pick deterministic. Ungated: VFEP is a hard
    dependency, so the def is always there and a renamed one would log a patch error at every
    boot, which is why Tests/1.6/CompatPatchTests.cs expects no main-tree hit for it. Combat
    Extended's own patch on the gun (PatchOperationMakeGunCECompatible) adds no tags of its
    own to this one and replaces none, so the tag survives CE in either load order.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName = "VFEP_WarcasketGun_Minigun"]/weaponTags</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>MDWC_StrangerInBlack</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
